& [IR5SurfaceBoundaryImportAndInvariantReconciliationV1] is the IR5-S01 boundary map for surface projection prototype planning
  + [boundary_map_id] is ir5-surface-boundary-import-and-invariant-reconciliation-v1
  + [boundary_map_uuid] is 356d5da6-22dd-443c-9c12-7b381f3333b3
  + [slice_id] is IR5-S01
  + [source_chunk] is IR5 surface projection prototype
  + [authority_scope] is imported FSC4 projection contracts, imported FSC5 safety contracts, imported IR4 runtime proof, projection authority ladder, generated-output non-authority boundary, operations dry-run handoff, stale triggers, and forbidden mutation boundaries
  + [implementation_scope] is boundary import and invariant reconciliation only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: import accepted surface, operations, and runtime-proof boundaries before defining authority display or projection-state contracts
  = must: preserve every projected surface as a view over accepted SOP records, accepted proofs, completion reviews, and generated projection evidence
  = must: keep runtime graph state, checkpoints, traces, generated reports, surface state, adapter state, chat state, terminal output, IRC logs, Matrix events, web events, Langflow diagrams, and Codex thread state non-authoritative
  = must: preserve dry-run-only operations semantics and live-control refusal when operation-like requests originate from any surface
  - never: implement executable UI, adapter code, fixture files, expected ledgers, generated output writers, dependency installation, operations simulator code, operations control, or live machine control in this slice

