& [ReconciledIR5InvariantSet] is the reconciled invariant set for IR5 surface projection prototype planning
  + [invariant] is SOP source documents, accepted canonical specifications, accepted packs, accepted proofs, accepted completion reviews, accepted human override records, and SJS-signed artifacts remain source authority
  + [invariant] is surface projection records are derived views and never source authority by themselves
  + [invariant] is projection_id, projection_kind, source_record_ref_set, lineage_edge_set, authority_notice_ref, freshness_state, projected_status, invalidation_ref_set, supported_action_route_set, forbidden_action_set, and mutation_boundary_ref are required for decision-making projections
  + [invariant] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, conversation, adapter, web, IRC, Matrix, terminal, Codex, and Langflow carriers may display readiness or intent but cannot assign, dispatch, accept completion, mutate source authority, or open gates
  + [invariant] is inbound user or agent actions from any carrier must be classified before an authority-sensitive route can run
  + [invariant] is unsupported, ambiguous, stale, contested, blocked, faulted, or interrupted action context routes to SOP-first interrupt or completion review, not silent mutation
  + [invariant] is IR4 runtime graph state, checkpoints, traces, terminal outcomes, fixture outputs, generated reports, and generated projections are execution evidence or projection evidence only
  + [invariant] is every runtime-derived projection consumed by IR5 must carry lower-authority notice, freshness state, source lineage, generated_at, and invalidation references
  + [invariant] is operation-like requests originating from surfaces are operation request records, dry-run result records, refusal records, or safety review requests only
  + [invariant] is dry-run success, fixture success, broad approval, projected user intent, or FSC5 acceptance cannot authorize live control
  + [invariant] is multi-surface divergence produces stale, contested, divergence notice, coordination conflict, or SOP-first interrupt output before follow-on action
  + [invariant] is generated-output roots, fixture roots, expected ledgers, adapter queues, and surface caches stay outside source authority unless a later accepted slice explicitly defines a bounded generated-output policy

  = must: preserve these invariants through IR5-S02 through IR5-S05
  = must: route invariant contradictions through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

& [ProjectionAuthorityLadder: IR5] is the authority ladder that all downstream IR5 projections must preserve
  + [authority_tier] is source_authority
  + [source_authority_member] is preserved source specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted canonical specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted SJS satisfaction signature
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted proof pack
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted completion review
  + [source_authority_member] is explicit accepted human override record with authority notice
  + [authority_tier] is accepted_execution_evidence
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is operator_trace accepted through proof or completion review
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is no_hidden_write proof accepted through proof or completion review
  + [authority_tier] is generated_projection_evidence
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is runtime graph terminal outcome
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is checkpoint record
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated trace
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated report
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is fixture output
  + [authority_tier] is carrier_context
  + [carrier_context_member] is chat message
  + [carrier_context_member] is Codex thread state
  + [carrier_context_member] is terminal output
  + [carrier_context_member] is IRC log
  + [carrier_context_member] is Matrix event
  + [carrier_context_member] is web request state
  + [carrier_context_member] is Langflow diagram

  = must: display lower authority tier and trust limit anywhere lower-tier records may influence action
  = must: prevent lower tiers from satisfying source-authority obligations without accepted promotion through proof, SJS, human override, or completion review

& [SurfaceProjectionBoundaryImportMap: IR5] is the imported surface contract map for downstream IR5 projection work
  + [projection_family] is manager projection imports ManagerProjectionContract, AuthorityNoticeContract, FreshnessDisplayRule, FalseReadyPreventionRule, completion review state, and IR5 work state
  + [projection_family] is worker projection imports WorkerPacketProjectionContract, authority notice, model route, forbidden scope, verification oracle, coordination claims, and completion review requirement
  + [projection_family] is narrative projection imports NarrativeProjectionContract, CompactionReentryProjectionRule, unresolved frontier display, completion review lineage, and stale trigger set
  + [projection_family] is debug projection imports DebugProjectionContract, OperatorTraceInspectionRule, fault visibility, checkpoint authority boundary, and generated-output non-authority status
  + [projection_family] is conversation projection imports ConversationProjectionContract, participant identity, conversation lineage, authority notice, freshness state, blocked or interrupted state, and available action routes
  + [projection_family] is adapter projection imports AdapterProjectionContractSet, InboundActionClassificationRule, OutboundProjectionRule, AdapterMutationThroughOperatorGate, MultiSurfaceDivergenceRule, and CarrierContextRule
  + [projection_family] is Langflow projection imports adapter projection rules and remains explanatory_projection_only unless a future accepted slice grants a different route
  + [projection_family] is operations-request projection imports OperationRequestSchema, DryRunResultSchema, RefusalOutputContract, MachineControlNonAuthorityRule, and LiveControlProhibitionGate

  = must: require IR5-S02 to define the display and projection-state contract before fixtures, executable surface code, adapter code, or generated outputs are created
  = must: refuse any projection family that cannot preserve authority notice, freshness, lineage, and stop-state visibility

& [IR4RuntimeProofHandoffForIR5] is the handoff from accepted IR4 runtime graph implementation proof into IR5 surface projection planning
  + [handoff_source] is IR4LangGraphProofRuntimeImplementationProofPackV1
  + [usable_evidence] is graph contract models for state and authority validation
  + [usable_evidence] is checkpoint validators that classify current, stale, authority-confused, and false-readiness states
  + [usable_evidence] is SOP-first interrupt context records for authority-sensitive pauses
  + [usable_evidence] is pure graph runner terminal outcomes
  + [usable_evidence] is fixture runner proof that source and expected-ledger roots are protected
  + [handoff_limit] is runtime proof may inform projection state but may not become source authority, dispatch authority, adapter authority, operation authority, or live-control authority

  = must: show runtime-derived terminal_success, terminal_blocked, terminal_stale, terminal_fault, and terminal_interrupt as generated projection evidence unless accepted by completion review
  = must: fault or interrupt any future surface that treats checkpoint state as readiness authority

& [OperationsSafetyHandoffForIR5] is the handoff from accepted FSC5 operations safety into IR5 surface projection planning
  + [handoff_source] is FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1
  + [usable_evidence] is operation request schema
  + [usable_evidence] is intended effect classification
  + [usable_evidence] is resource target classification
  + [usable_evidence] is dry-run result schema
  + [usable_evidence] is refusal output contract
  + [usable_evidence] is machine-control non-authority rule
  + [usable_evidence] is live-control prohibition gate
  + [handoff_limit] is surfaces may display or request dry-run planning records only; no command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, or live machine control is authorized

  = must: convert operation-like requests from carriers into classified requests, refusal records, or SOP-first interrupt contexts
  = must: keep human approval display separate from live-control permission until a separate future live-control authority is source-preserved, SJS-processed, and accepted

& [IR5GeneratedOutputAndFixtureBoundary] is the generated-output and fixture boundary for IR5-S01
  + [fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_projection_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [future_fixture_slice] is IR5-S03 after IR5-S01 and IR5-S02 acceptance
  + [future_generated_output_policy_slice] is IR5-S04 after IR5-S03 acceptance
  + [current_generated_output_role] is none_created_by_this_slice
  + [future_generated_output_default_authority] is non_authoritative_projection_only

  = must: reject IR5-S01 completion if fixture sources, expected ledgers, generated output files, surface caches, adapter queues, or projection reports are created
  = must: require later accepted generated-output policy before any generated projection root can be trusted even as disposable evidence

& [ForbiddenIR5S01MutationList] is the forbidden mutation set for IR5-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC4, FSC5, IR4, or IR5 authority inputs to make reconciliation easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating surface state as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating adapter or carrier state as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating runtime graph state, checkpoint state, generated traces, generated reports, or fixture outputs as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is omitting authority_notice, freshness_state, lineage, or stop-state visibility from a decision-making projection contract
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing executable UI components
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing adapters, transports, queues, sockets, or Langflow export
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing dependencies or mutating package metadata
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating fixture source files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating expected ledger files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating generated output files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing operations simulator code
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching agents, jobs, commands, processes, GPU work, model runtimes, or persistent operations automation
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control

  = must: fail IR5-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR5] is the stale trigger set for downstream IR5 work
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 canonical specification hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 minting review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC4 surface projection pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC5 operations safety pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR4 runtime graph implementation proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is authority notice contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is conversation or adapter projection contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is operations safety or live-control prohibition contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR4 runtime checkpoint or interrupt policy changes
  + [stale_trigger] is missing authority_notice detected in downstream display contract
  + [stale_trigger] is hidden blocked, stale, faulted, interrupted, contested, or pending-review state detected
  + [stale_trigger] is generated projection, carrier context, checkpoint, trace, report, dry-run, fixture result, or human approval display treated as source authority
  + [stale_trigger] is operation-like projection treated as permission for command execution or live-control effect
  + [stale_trigger] is multi-surface divergence without stale, conflict, or interrupt output

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

